---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import TimelineSlider from '../components/TimelineSlider.astro';
import GatedDownload from '../components/GatedDownload.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { ownFaqs } from '../data/faqs';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';
import { getLivePost } from '../lib/content';
const rentOwn = await getLivePost('renting-vs-owning-professional-corporation');
const months = [
  ['Month 1', 'Your PC is formed in launch states. Physician owner matched. Clinicians roster-added under Anvil\'s contracts. You are billing.'],
  ['Months 1-4', 'Credentialing files built under your entity. Contract applications filed in your PC\'s name with your top payers.'],
  ['Months 4-8', 'First commercial contracts effective. New visits with those payers route to your PC. Claims in flight are unaffected.'],
  ['Months 8-12', 'Medicaid MCO and remaining commercial contracts land. Majority of volume on your own contracts. Platform fee steps down.'],
  ['Months 12-18', 'Steady state. Anvil runs RCM and renewals on contracts you own. Rental PC stays available for new states and closed panels.'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Own your contracts vs network rental" description="Network rental means renting your revenue. Anvil launches you on a rented PC and migrates you to contracts your own entity holds, over 6 to 18 months, with no revenue gap." jsonLd={[breadcrumbJsonLd([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Own your contracts', path: '/own-your-contracts' }])]}>
  <Hero compact eyebrow="Own your contracts" title="If your vendor owns your payer contracts, you don't have insurance revenue. You have a lease." sub="Own your payer contracts instead of staying on network rental. Forward this to your board: what network rental vs owning contracts actually means, why rental is the right way to launch, and why it is the wrong place to stay." secondary={{ label: 'See pricing', href: '/pricing' }} />

  <Section eyebrow="The problem" title="Network rental is renting your revenue">
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <div class="card"><h3>You never hold the contract</h3><p class="muted">The payer contracts, rates, and relationships sit in the vendor's entity. If you leave, you start from zero. Your entire insured revenue runs through a company you do not control.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>You never see the rate</h3><p class="muted">You are paid a lease fee, not the contracted rate. You cannot negotiate with a payer. You cannot see the ladder. You cannot tell whether the fee is fair.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>One vendor, one point of failure</h3><p class="muted">A payer terminating the vendor's group contract terminates every customer's coverage with that payer at once. That is concentration risk your investors will ask about.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:32px">Renting is still the fastest way to launch. The mistake is treating it as the destination. {rentOwn ? <>Read <a href={`/resources/${rentOwn.id}`}>rent a PC vs own a PC</a>, then compare</> : <>Compare</>} the model on <a href="/compare/bridge">Anvil vs Bridge</a>, see how we paper <a href="/platform/compliance">CPOM and AKS</a>, or start from <a href="/solutions/switching">switching from a network rental vendor</a>.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="The migration" title="How volume moves from our PC to yours" intro="Both tracks start on day one. Nothing about the migration gates your launch or interrupts billing.">
    <div class="steps">
      {months.map(([when, what]) => (
        <div class="step reveal"><div class="when">{when}</div><p>{what}</p></div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:32px"><TimelineSlider /></div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="What you end up with" title="An asset, not a dependency" tight>
    <ul class="check-list two-col">
      <li>Your own professional corporation in every state you operate</li>
      <li>A licensed physician owner under a friendly-PC structure</li>
      <li>Executed MSO and PC agreements, structured for each state's CPOM rules. See <a href="/platform/compliance">MSO-PC and corporate practice of medicine</a>.</li>
      <li>Payer contracts in your entity's name, with portable payer contracts and billing under your own entity</li>
      <li>Credentialing files for every clinician, portable</li>
      <li>Reporting by payer, state, clinician, and code, under your entity</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Diligence" title="What investors ask, and what the answer should be">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>On rental forever</th><th>After migration</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Does insured revenue run through an entity you control?</td><td class="muted">No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Are payer contracts assignable in a sale?</td><td class="muted">There are none to assign</td><td>Yes, they are the company's</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Can a single vendor terminate network access?</td><td class="muted">Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Do you know your contracted rates?</td><td class="muted">No, lease fee only</td><td>Yes, by payer and code</td></tr>
            <tr><td>What is the switching cost?</td><td class="muted">A relaunch</td><td>A vendor change</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <GatedDownload name="diligence-checklist" title="Payer contract diligence checklist" body="The twelve questions we would ask any care company about its insurance revenue, with the answer that passes. Built for Series A and B diligence." cta="Send me the checklist" />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Cost" title="Renting forever vs owning by year one" tight>
    <p class="lede">Rental fees do not step down. Ownership fees do. Run both on your numbers in the <a href="/pricing#calculator">calculator</a>{rentOwn && <>, or read the <a href={`/resources/${rentOwn.id}`}>full comparison</a></>}.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section tight><Faq items={ownFaqs} /></Section>
  <CtaBand title="Rent for speed. Own for the asset. Start both today." body="Tell us your states and clinicians. We will map the migration month by month." primary={{ label: 'Get started', href: '/contact?src=own' }} secondary={{ label: 'See pricing', href: '/pricing' }} />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 12px; }
  .step { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 18px; }
  .step .when { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .step p { margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .two-col { columns: 2; column-gap: 32px; max-width: 900px; }
  .two-col li { break-inside: avoid; }
  @media (max-width: 960px) { .steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .steps, .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; columns: 1; } }
</style>
